  abstract = "We present the first extension of the special-relativistic
              Lattice-Boltzmann Method for radiative transport developed by Weih
              et al. (2020), to solve the radiative-transfer equation in curved
              spacetimes. The novel approach is based on the streaming of
              carefully selected photons along null geodesics and interpolating
              their final positions, velocities, and frequency shifts to all
              photons in a given velocity stencil. Furthermore, by transforming
              between the laboratory frame, the Eulerian frame, and the fluid
              frame, we are able to perform the collision step in the fluid
              frame, thus retaining the collision operator of the
              special-relativistic case with only minor modifications. As a
